+++ b/specs/005-create-patch/spec.md
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Spec: createPatch
+
+**Standards**: JSON Patch, RFC 6902 §4 (add, remove, replace; §4.6 equality) with paths as JSON Pointers,
+RFC 6901 §3, §4 (`~` is escaped `~0`, `/` is `~1`). Constitution I names these sections.
+
+`createPatch(from, to)` returns a JSON Patch such that `applyPatch(from, createPatch(from, to))` equals `to`.
+
+- Equal documents (RFC 6902 §4.6 equality) give `[]`.
+- Objects are compared member by member, recursively: removed members give `remove`, new members `add`,
+  changed members recurse. A change of type (object/array/primitive/null) or of a primitive gives `replace`
+  at that path (path `""` for the root).
+- Arrays: items are aligned by longest common subsequence of equal items. An inserted item gives one `add`
+  and a deleted item one `remove`; surrounding items are not touched. A moved item is a `remove` plus an `add`
+  (no `move`, no rewriting of the items in between). Unaligned items at the same position that differ are
+  diffed recursively rather than replaced.
+- Indices in operations are valid against the document as already modified by earlier operations.
+- Neither input is mutated; values in the patch are copies sharing no structure with the inputs.
+  `__proto__` keys are handled as ordinary members.
